course: dictionary
lesson: 3827
title: One word, many shapes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Formation comes from the word form, which means to make or shape something. A formation is the way something is made, or a pattern that things are arranged in. Context tells you which meaning is right.
explain: «In the testudo, or tortoise formation, soldiers locked their shields above and around them to protect against arrows.» Here formation is a shape that people stand in. The clues are locked shields and protect against arrows, so it must mean a planned arrangement.
explain: Formation can also mean how something forms over time, as in the formation of clouds or caves. Try your meaning in the sentence: «The formation of the club took a year» means the setting up of the club. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Formation means the way something is made or forms over time.
fact: A formation is a pattern or shape that people, planes, birds or players are arranged in.
fact: A rock formation is a natural shape or group of rocks.
fact: «Back-formation» means making a new word by chopping off what looks like an ending: «burgle» was made from «burglar», and «edit» from «editor».
fact: Useful phrases: in formation, cloud formation, the formation of.
exercise: «In the testudo, or tortoise formation, soldiers locked their shields above and around them.» What is a formation here? | A type of weather | A sort of tent | *A shape people are arranged in, to protect themselves | A kind of tortoise
exercise: In back-formation, «burgle» was made by chopping an ending off which word? | burgle | burgers | *burglar | brilliant
exercise: In science, what is the formation of a cave? | A kind of map of the cave | A party held inside the cave | *How the cave is made over time | A type of rock
test: «The aircraft flew in formation over the crowd at the air show.» What does formation mean here? | A loud noise | *An arrangement or pattern of planes | A broken engine | A kind of cloud
test: «The formation of the new club took three months.» What does formation mean here? | Its shape on the pitch | Its colours | A map of the town | *The setting up of the club
exam: Which best describes a rock formation? | *A natural shape or group of rocks | A path up a mountain | A kind of rock song | A building made by people
